# text = His head was soon in a basin of water , and out of it again , and staring at her through a storm of towelling towelling at himself as if he were his bitterest enemy More serious of face , and more slow of action , than he had been , the boy completed his dressing , and came and sat down at the little breakfast-table , with his eyes amazedly directed to her face In spite of her unchanged manner of speaking , and her unchanged appearance of composure , she scarcely trusted herself to look at him , but kept her eyes employed on the cutting and buttering of his bread , and on the mixing of his tea , and other such little preparations grumbled the boy , throwing his bread and butter about , in an ill-humour .
