# text = Mr Lightwood , without explaining that his weariness was chronic , proceeded with his exposition that , all forms of law having been at length complied with , will of Harmon deceased having been proved , death of Harmon next inheriting having been proved , & amp ; c ., and so forth , Court of Chancery having been moved , & amp ; c . and so forth , he , Mr Lightwood , had now the gratification , honour , and happiness , again & amp ; c . and so forth , of congratulating Mr Boffin on coming into possession as residuary legatee , of upwards of one hundred thousand pounds , standing in the books of the Governor and Company of the Bank of England , again & amp ; c . and so forth concluded Mr Lightwood , with an indolent smile Without following this last remark very closely , Mr Boffin cast his perplexed gaze first at the ceiling , and then at the carpet he remarked said that gentleman returned Mortimer retorted Mr Boffin , still perplexed asked Mortimer , raising his eyebrows answered Mr Boffin , with a wistful look said Mr Boffin , rubbing his ear making the discovery all of a sudden Mr Lightwood coughed , not convinced pursued Mr Boffin Mr Lightwood murmured pursued Mr Boffin said Mr Boffin lowering his voice Mr Lightwood murmured said Mr Boffin , warming ( as fat usually does ) with a tendency to melt said Mortimer , with a light laugh returned Mr Boffin , on whom his manner seemed to grate observed Lightwood said Mr Boffin , pausing remarked Lightwood , with a languid inclination of the head returned Lightwood said Mr Boffin , a little staggered returned Lightwood , making a very short note of it with a very rusty pen At some loss to fathom Mr Boffin's notions of a tight will , Lightwood felt his way Mr Boffin explained interposed her husband repeated Mr Boffin , with a short sturdy laugh So that instruction , too , was taken by Mr Lightwood ; and Mr Lightwood , having taken it , was in the act of showing Mr Boffin out , when Mr Eugene Wrayburn almost jostled him in the door - way .
