# text = And so departed , without looking back Betaking himself straight homeward , Mr Boffin , without further let or hindrance , arrived at the Bower , and gave Mrs Boffin ( in a walking dress of black velvet and feathers , like a mourning coach - horse ) an account of all he had said and done since breakfast he then pursued said Mrs Boffin , smoothing her dress with an air of immense enjoyment cried Mrs Boffin , laughing with the glee of a child returned her husband said the cheerfial Mrs Boffin Mr Boffin hinted Mr Boffin , who had a deep respect for his wife's intuitive wisdom , replied , though rather pensively said Mrs Boffin Mr Boffin assented , with his former pensiveness , as he took his seat upon his settle Mrs Boffin , a smiling creature , broad of figure and simple of nature , with her hands folded in her lap , and with buxom creases in her throat , proceeded to expound her views assented the still pensive Mr Boffin exclaimed Mrs Boffin , laughing and clapping her hands , and gaily rocking herself to and fro cried the delighted creature Mrs Boffin clapped her hands again , rocked herself again , beat her feet upon the floor , and wiped the tears of laughter from her eyes inquired Mr Boffin , when he also had sympathetically laughed said Mrs Boffin , coming from her fashionable sofa to his side on the plain settle , and hooking her comfortable arm through his cried Mr Boffin , smiting the table in his admiration Mrs Boffin pulled his nearest ear , in acknowledgment of this piece of philosophy , and then said , gradually toning down to a motherly strain interposed her husband her husband interposed again said Mrs Boffin , once more radiant in her comely way from head to foot , and once more smoothing her dress with immense enjoyment said her husband
