# text = For , the poor little harmless gentleman once had his fancy , like the rest of us , and she didn't answer ( as she often does not ), and he thinks the adorable bridesmaid is like the fancy as she was then ( which she is not at all ), and that if the fancy had not married some one else for money , but had married him for love , he and she would have been happy ( which they wouldn't have been ), and that she has a tenderness for him still ( whereas her toughness is a proverb ).
