# text = Miss Podsnap's early views of life being principally derived from the reflections of it in her father's boots , and in the walnut and rosewood tables of the dim drawing - rooms , and in their swarthy giants of looking-glasses , were of a sombre cast ; and it was not wonderful that now , when she was on most days solemnly tooled through the Park by the side of her mother in a great tall custard-coloured phaeton , she showed above the apron of that vehicle like a dejected young person sitting up in bed to take a startled look at things in general , and very strongly desiring to get her head under the counterpane again .
