# text = Even this general's career paled in interest for Mr Boffin before the clearing of his conscience with Wegg ; and hence , when that literary gentleman had according to custom eaten and drunk until he was all a-glow , and when he took up his book with the usual chirping introduction Mr Boffin stopped him replied that gentleman , turning the open book face downward as if there were the least necessity with a feint of taking up the book Mr Wegg ( who had had nothing else in his mind for several nights ) took off his spectacles with an air of bland surprise returned that reticent individual This , as a philanthropic aspiration said Mr Boffin replied Wegg said Mr Boffin .
