# text = These , in the days of their abundance , ever regarded gold as dross , and have not yet got over that only impediment in the way of their amassing wealth , but they want no dross from Nicodemus Boffin , Esquire ; No , Mr Boffin ; the world may term it pride , paltry pride if you will , but they wouldn't take it if you offered it ; a loan , sir -- for fourteen weeks to the day , interest calculated at the rate of five per cent per annum , to be bestowed upon any charitable institution you may name -- is all they want of you , and if you have the meanness to refuse it , count on being despised by these great spirits .
