# text = The legal gentleman is at the Pocket-Breaches Branch Station , with an open carriage with a printed bill ' Veneering for ever ' stuck upon it , as if it were a wall ; and they gloriously proceed , amidst the grins of the populace , to a feeble little town hall on crutches , with some onions and bootlaces under it , which the legal gentleman says are a Market ; and from the front window of that edifice Veneering speaks to the listening earth .
