# text = But the Temple , accustomed to tone down both the still life and the human life that has much to do with it , would soon get the better of all that said Eugene , on one side of the fire asked Lightwood , from the other side of the fire pursued Eugene , reflecting said Mortimer returned Eugene , indolently surprised said Mortimer , in a slightly injured tone retorted Eugene His friend , lying back in his easy chair , watched him lying back in his easy chair , as he stretched out his legs on the hearth-rug , and said , with the amused look that Eugene Wrayburn could always awaken in him without seeming to try or care exclaimed Eugene , raising his eyes to the ceiling said Mortimer returned his friend , lazily lifting his head a little to look at him exclaimed Lightwood , laughing said Eugene , getting out of his chair with much gravity With that , taking up a candle , he conducted his chum into the fourth room of the set of chambers -- a little narrow room -- which was very completely and neatly fitted as a kitchen said Eugene sitting on his bed , with the air of a philosopher lecturing a disciple Mortimer laughed again , with his usual commentaries of and but when his laugh was out , there was something serious , if not anxious , in his face .
