# text = But does not openly growl says Venus , politely handing it over says Wegg says Wegg , shaking his head asks Venus says Venus , reddening and growing something louder Mr Wegg suggests , pacifically As Mr Venus is irritable ( no doubt owing to his disappointment in love ), and as it is not the cue of Mr Wegg to have him out of temper , the latter gentleman soothingly remarks , ' I only put it as a little case ; I only put it ha'porthetically is Mr Venus's retort Arrived by this time in Mr Wegg's sitting-room , made bright on the chilly evening by gaslight and fire , Mr Venus softens and compliments him on his abode ; profiting by the occasion to remind Wegg that he ( Venus ) told him he had got into a good thing Wegg rejoins returns the other So , Mr Venus mixes , and Wegg mixes ; and Mr Venus lights and puffs , and Wegg lights and puffs returns Wegg returns that gentleman Having said which , Mr Wegg smokes and looks at the fire with a most determined expression of Charity ; as if he had caught that cardinal virtue by the skirts as she felt it her painful duty to depart from him , and held her by main force resumes Wegg pursues Silas , with an oratorical flourish of his pipe and his wooden leg : the latter having an undignified tendency to tilt him back in his chair Mr Venus murmurs that he does say so Mr Wegg rolls his eyes all round the room , in that ever unsatisfied quest of his , and then rolls his eyes all round Mr Venus ; as if suspicious of his having something about him to be found out he pursues
