# text = On each occasion of his saying ' mix again ', Mr Wegg , with a hop on his wooden leg , hitches his chair a little nearer ; more as if he were proposing that himself and Mr Venus should mix again , than that they should replenish their glasses says Wegg when the other has acted on his hospitable entreaty Mr Wegg claps on his spectacles , and admiringly surveys Mr Venus from head to foot says Wegg , holding Mr Venus's palm out , flat and ready for smiting , and now smiting it cries Wegg ; and the apostrophe is not the less impressive for the Being's hand being actually upon his rum and water slowly returns that practical anatomist , after drinking says Mr Wegg , again holding out Mr Venus's palm as if he were going to tell his fortune by chiromancy , and holding his own up ready for smiting it when the time should come ; ' as one that the poet might have had his eye on , in writing the national naval words :
