# text = And as she had never been sparing of complaints of her old home when she had no other to compare it with , so there was no novelty of ingratitude or disdain in her very much preferring her new one said Mr Boffin , after some two or three months Neither could Bella , so she found the subject rather interesting said Mr Boffin inquired Bella said Mr Boffin said Miss Bella , with an airy toss of her head replied Mr Boffin , thinking it over suggested Bella repeated Mr Boffin , with a shake of his head , after again thinking it over asked Bella said Mr Boffin Oho ! thought Miss Bella For Mr Mortimer Lightwood had dined there two or three times , and she had met him elsewhere , and he had shown her some attention That Pa's daughter should be so contemptuous of Pa's lodger was odd ; but there were odder anomalies than that in the mind of the spoilt girl : spoilt first by poverty , and then by wealth .
