# text = He appeared before the dolls' dressmaker , sitting alone at her work thought that sharp young personage said Bradley Headstone returned Miss Wren returned Miss Wren Bradley glanced distrustfully at the shrewd face again bending over the work , and said , trying to conquer doubt and hesitation returned Miss Wren , snapping her fingers in a volley of impatient snaps Miss Wren wrinkled her nose , to express dislike replied Miss Wren , with a shrug and a laugh said Bradley , returning to the accusation , a little injured returned the little creature Bradley glanced at the doll she held up for his observation -- which had been lying on its face on her bench , while with a needle and thread she fastened the dress on at the back -- and looked from it to her pursued Miss Wren , doing so , and making two little dabs at him in the air with her needle , as if she pricked him with it in his own eyes retorted Miss Wren , hitching her chin exclaimed Miss Wren pursued Bradley , half humouring what was present , and half angry with what was not present exclaimed the dressmaker repeated Bradley , warming remarked the dressmaker She had hardly done so , when Lizzie Hexam arrived , and showed some surprise on seeing Bradley Headstone there , and Jenny shaking her little fist at him close before her eyes , and the Honourable Mrs T . with her face to the wall said the knowing Miss Wren Lizzie took the hand which the dolls' dressmaker held out to her for the purpose of being supported away , but only looked at her with an inquiring smile , and made no other movement said Miss Wren returned Lizzie , releasing the hand , and laying her own lightly on Miss Jenny's curls .
