# text = If they owed a duty to Betty Higden , of a surety that duty must be done said Mrs Boffin , when she accompanied John Rokesmith back to his room , and shone upon her with the light of her radiant face , ' granted all else , I think I wouldn't run away said Mrs Higden , shaking her head was the bright and ready answer Betty thanked him with a grateful curtsey said Betty , with logical good faith asked Mrs Boffin , still reluctant , of the Secretary After more discussion it was agreed that it should be done , and Mrs Boffin summoned Bella to note down the little purchases that were necessary to set Betty up in trade said the stanch old heart , observant of Bella's face : when I take my seat with my work , clean and busy and fresh , in a country market-place , I shall turn a sixpence as sure as ever a farmer's wife there .'
