# text = She moved slowly on when he paused , and he moved slowly on beside her he resumed She started at the passionate sound of the last words , and at the passionate action of his hands , with which they were accompanied A touch of pity for him mingled with her dislike of him , and she said he cried , despairingly Struggling with himself , and by times looking up at the deserted windows of the houses as if there could be anything written in their grimy panes that would help him , he paced the whole pavement at her side , before he spoke again said Lizzie , with her eyes upon the ground asked Lizzie Hexam he said , always speaking passionately , and , when most emphatic , repeating that former action of his hands , which was like flinging his heart's blood down before her in drops upon the pavement-stones
