# text = The dimples duly tied up in the bonnet - strings and the leave-taking done , they got out into the air , and the cherub drew a long breath as if he found it refreshing said Bella returned the cherub Bella drew his arm closer through hers as they walked along , and gave it a number of consolatory pats he said , as if she had spoken said the cherub Pa laughing at this , Bella gave him two or three shakes Bella laid the little forefinger of her right glove on her lip , and then laid it on her father's lip said her father , settling her arm comfortably and confidentially said Bella she was confused here in spite of her merry way of beginning Pa looked in her face , and looked at the ground , and looked in her face again , and declared he could never guess said Bella separating the syllables for emphasis Pa answered quietly with the counter-question returned Bella sharply said her father , meditating said Bella remarked Bella , with a touch of her mother's loftiness Bella again saying , with her former emphasis her father felt himself bound to echo said Bella her father interposed rejoined Bella , giving him another shake or two said the cherub , a little depressed Here the grateful girl burst out crying very heartily said her father , with his hand to his eyes
