# text = the women asked her said Betty They assisted her to rise , but she could not stand yet , and they supported her when she sat down again upon the bench said old Betty , leaning her face drowsily on the breast of the woman who had spoken before said some farmers standing by , who had come out from their market-dinner said the woman answered Betty But are any of 'em near here ? ' said the men's voices ; the women's voices chiming in when it was said , and prolonging the strain said Betty , rousing herself was the next compassionate chorus she heard said Betty , rising with difficulty A well-meaning bystander , yellow-legginged and purple-faced , said hoarsely over his red comforter , as she rose to her feet , that she ' oughtn't to be let to go cried old Betty , all her fears crowding on her She caught up her basket as she spoke and was making an unsteady rush away from them , when the same bystander checked her with his hand on her sleeve , and urged her to come with him and see the parish-doctor .
