# text = Eugene drew a chair to the fire by which he was having his wine and reading the evening paper , and brought a glass , and filled it for good fellowship's sake replied Wrayburn said Eugene thoughtfully returned the debtor , very composedly taking up his glass said Eugene , pausing in setting down his glass said Eugene returned Lightwood said Lightwood , laughing remarked Eugene with much gravity returned Lightwood impatiently observed Eugene , turning round to the furniture Eugene Wrayburn rose , and put his hands in his pockets , and stood with a foot on the fender , indolently rocking his body and looking at the fire .
