# text = In a minute or two he resumed his chair , as perfectly unconcerned as usual , and rallied his friend on having so narrowly escaped the prowess of their muscular visitor said Mortimer , restlessly cried Eugene said Mortimer exclaimed Eugene , airily said Mortimer , after lighting a cigar , and comforting himself with a whiff or two Lightwood took his cigar from his lips in surprise , and looked at his friend , as if with a latent suspicion that there must be a jest or hidden meaning in his words said Wrayburn , answering the look and smiling carelessly remarked Eugene , turning round to the furniture again , with an air of indolent rapture asked Lightwood , opposing a serious face to the laugh of his friend observed Lightwood , who had heard it out with serious attention said Eugene returned Eugene with the calmest indifference Lightwood hesitated ; but , yielding to his curiosity , rose cried Eugene , rising too said Mortimer , laughing through his gravity
