# text = He set himself to find out , for the man might prove to be a messenger between those two he remarked , with a lumbering show of ease cried Mr Riderhood , with a hoarse laugh said Bradley , looking disconcertedly about him said Riderhood Bradley looked at him , as though he were claiming to be a Ghost said Mr Riderhood , obstinately asked Bradley , eyeing him with distrust growled Mr Riderhood , winding up his monotonous summary of his wrongs Bradley Headstone's face had changed during this latter recital , and he had observed the speaker with a more sustained attention said he , after a pause , during which they walked on side by side was the answer , accompanied with a stop and a stare returned that gentleman . '
