# text = The schoolmaster put his hand in his pocket , and produced two half-crowns , and placed them in Mr Riderhood's palm : who stopped at a convenient doorstep to ring them both , before acknowledging their receipt said Riderhood , faring on again when he had carefully pocketed the coins on that side of himself which was furthest from his new friend said Riderhood , as arguing something that was self-evident Bradley gave this answer in a stolid , vacant , and self-communing manner , which Mr Riderhood found very extraordinary said Bradley , coming to the name in a reluctant and forced way , as if he were dragged to it Riderhood nodded , and asked returned Mr Riderhood , bluntly returned Bradley with quivering lips cried Mr Riderhood said Riderhood , turning angry repeated Mr Riderhood , growing intentionally slower of comprehension as the other quickened in his speech The Rogue had got the clue he wanted , though he held it with a clumsy hand .
