# text = This repudiation was not only an act of deliberate policy on Fledgeby's part , in case of his being surprised by any other caller , but was also a retort upon Miss Wren for her over-sharpness , and a pleasant instance of his humour as regarded the old Jew This was Fledgeby's habitual reflection in the way of business , and it was sharpened just now by the old man's presuming to have a secret from him : though of the secret itself , as annoying somebody else whom he disliked , he by no means disapproved .
