# text = Returning to the breakfast-room , he found Mrs Lammle still standing on her side of the table , and Mr Lammle on his said Mr Boffin , showing the money and the necklace Mrs Lammle had taken up her parasol from a side table , and stood sketching with it on the pattern of the damask cloth , as she had sketched on the pattern of Mr Twemlow's papered wall she said , turning her head towards him , but not her eyes said Mr Boffin Mrs Lammle explained , in a measured voice , and with an emphasis on her last word he returned said Mrs Lammle , still sketching , and seeming to bestow great pains upon it said Mrs Boffin , in her ready good nature asked her husband , mockingly Mr Boffin interposed
