# text = Apparently with no compunction , and assuredly with no ceremony , Bella tossed her bonnet away , and sat down to make the tea Before Mrs Wilfer could wave her gloves , the Mendicant's bride in her merriest affectionate manner went on again here her eyes sparkled more brightly Having got up and kissed them again , she slipped back to her chair ( after a loop on the road to squeeze her husband round the neck ) and again went on said her husband , smiling , as he stood by her side , without her having detected his approach But Bella started up , and put her hand upon his lips said John said John , with a very expressive look of admiration around him She laid her laughing cheek upon his breast to thank him , and said , looking at the rest of them sideways out of her bright eyes Even Mrs Wilfer relaxed under the influence of her married daughter , and seemed in a majestic manner to imply remotely that if R . W . had been a more deserving object , she too might have condescended to come down from her pedestal for his beguilement .
