# text = The hand and the match and the voice were then seen by John Rokesmith to belong to Mr Inspector , once meditatively active in this chronicle said Mr Inspector , in a business-like manner Mr Inspector , in a dark-blue buttoned-up frock coat and pantaloons , presented a serviceable , half-pay , Royal Arms kind of appearance , as he applied his pocket handkerchief to his nose and bowed to the lady said Mr Inspector was the reply retorted Mr Inspector , again using his pocket handkerchief Mr Inspector hinted her husband was beginning ; when Mr Inspector , regarding the words as an introduction , said And bowed , with gallantry resumed her husband said Mr Inspector When Mr Inspector put it in that other form there was a relishing roll in his voice , and his eye beamed with an official lustre inquired John Rokesmith , very coolly returned Mr Inspector in a comfortable sort of remonstrance Lord bless my soul and body !' returned Mr Inspector said Mr Inspector , shaking his head reproachfully said Mr Inspector said Mr Inspector With a reassuring kiss on the lips of the frightened Bella , her husband ( to whom Mr Inspector obligingly offered his arm ), took up a candle , and withdrew with that gentleman .
