# text = For all these reasons , when he and she and John , at towards nine o'clock of a winter evening went to London , and began driving from London Bridge , among low-lying water-side wharves and docks and strange places , Bella was in the state of a dreamer ; perfectly unable to account for her being there , perfectly unable to forecast what would happen next , or whither she was going , or why ; certain of nothing in the immediate present , but that she confided in John , and that John seemed somehow to be getting more triumphant .
