# text = This , and her husband's earnestness in explaining further to her how it had come to pass that he had been supposed to be slain , and had even been suspected of his own murder ; also , how he had put a pious fraud upon her which had preyed upon his mind , as the time for its disclosure approached , lest she might not make full allowance for the object with which it had originated , and in which it had fully developed cried Mrs Boflin , taking him up short at this point , with another hearty clap of her hands said Bella , looking vacantly from one to another exclaimed Mrs Boffin cried the comfortable creature , embracing her said John , laying his hand on hers cried Mrs Boffin Mr Boffin hitched up a chair , and added his broad brown right hand to the heap said Mrs Boffin , giving it a kiss her husband struck in Bella looked at him confusedly , and looked again at Mrs Boffin's radiant face said Mrs Boffin said Mr Boffin resumed Mrs Boffin ; ' stick to me .
